Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:22:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: RRC null integrity (EIA0) detector
 (T-OR-111 part a)

RrcNullIntegrityAnalyzer (default off) flags an RRC Security Mode Command
that selects the null integrity algorithm (EIA0), leaving access-stratum
signalling unauthenticated -- the AS-layer counterpart to the NAS Security
Mode Command EIA0 that the null_integrity analyzer already flags. A UE that
accepts it will act on forged RRC (measurement config, reconfiguration,
release/redirect), the foothold a false base station needs. High.

The one legitimate use of EIA0 is an unauthenticated emergency call;
suppressing that case (an EIA0 RRC SMC after an emergency attach) needs
connection state and is the remaining stateful part of T-OR-111, so an
emergency call is a known false positive until then -- hence off by default.

Test vectors are DL-DCCH SecurityModeCommand PDUs encoded with the reference
Python pycrate and decoded through telcom_parser: a Security Mode Command
selecting EIA0 (fires High), one selecting EIA2 (ignored), a benign
RRCConnectionReconfiguration (ignored), and a non-LTE element (ignored).

